 "text": "Hey there, how are you doing? You can wrap it in wet towels and slide it between layers of soft cushioning in the fridge. Keep it well wrapped and only open the lid a little at a time. blocks are better, they take up less space. Put them on top of something heavy, like water bottles, so they don't tip. Keep the cooler itself out of the fridge, it gets too hot and ruins the other food. Tell him to leave it alone and only open the door a few minutes before you get home. Pour it into fresh container and run it through the dishwasher just to be safe.",
